1
00:00:00,570 --> 00:00:04,009
♪ ♪

2
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:15,340
Alone, inexperienced,
life has never been tougher

3
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:18,340
for this young orangutan.

4
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:23,340
She will have to go
to extraordinary lengths

5
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:26,340
to find enough food.

6
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:37,760
A third of her kind will fall

7
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:41,760
and break bones or worse.

8
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:55,760
In this hostile world,
only the strongest

9
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:59,760
make it to the top.

10
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:26,960
Torrential rain, tropical heat
and the relentless assault of insects.

11
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:31,960
If you're not prepared,
the jungle will eat you alive.

12
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:35,960
But these conditions
have created a home

13
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:40,960
for more species than anywhere else
on the planet.

14
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:52,960
You might think
it's an animal Eden,

15
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:57,960
but it's more like
a wildlife war zone.

16
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:16,960
Now that the rains, the lifeblood
of these extraordinary worlds,

17
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:20,960
are becoming more unpredictable,

18
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:26,960
the battle for survival
has never been fiercer.

19
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:43,440
Even rainforests have dry seasons.

20
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:52,440
Rivers become the focus
of jungle life.

21
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:04,560
A jaguar,
South America's apex predator.

22
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,560
Jaguars will hunt anything

23
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:26,560
from a vulture to an anaconda.

24
00:03:57,560 --> 00:04:00,060
But nothing's guaranteed.

25
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:04,060
It's been days since she's eaten.

26
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:19,560
Jaguars are the most aquatic
of all big cats.

27
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:24,560
She'll have more success
in the water.

28
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,820
Capybara.

29
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,820
A big opportunity.

30
00:05:04,479 --> 00:05:10,479
There are other options,
but there's also competition.

31
00:05:16,479 --> 00:05:18,479
A male.

32
00:05:23,479 --> 00:05:28,479
He's hunted here
for over a decade,

33
00:05:28,479 --> 00:05:33,479
taking on dangerous prey
and other jaguars.

34
00:05:41,479 --> 00:05:46,479
Life here isn't getting
any easier.

35
00:05:51,479 --> 00:05:58,479
As dry seasons become more extreme,
competition for prey increases.

36
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:14,720
Better for her to hunt
in less contested waters

37
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:18,720
where prehistoric killers
lie waiting

38
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:22,720
to drag their victims under.

39
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:58,520
With each step,
a trap could snap shut.

40
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:02,000
With the right bite,
she'll pierce skull

41
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
and immobilize it.

42
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:18,000
But this caiman is much more
than a mouthful.

43
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:27,879
♪ ♪

44
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:37,240
A kill this big
has rarely been recorded.

45
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:41,240
It will feed her for days.

46
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:53,240
For other animals, finding food
at the height

47
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:59,240
of the dry season
is much more of a struggle.

48
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:12,040
Fruit makes up around 60%
of this young orangutan's diet.

49
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:17,040
To survive, she must form
a complex mental map

50
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:21,040
of where and when to find it.

51
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:28,040
This takes years.

52
00:09:30,890 --> 00:09:35,890
Up here,
there's nothing but leaves.

53
00:09:35,890 --> 00:09:40,890
Rainfall has dropped by a third.

54
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:44,890
And droughts are more frequent.

55
00:09:52,890 --> 00:09:57,890
How can she predict
where to find food

56
00:09:57,890 --> 00:10:02,890
when the world around her
keeps changing?

57
00:10:07,890 --> 00:10:13,890
The more she searches,
the more she risks.

58
00:10:18,130 --> 00:10:24,600
♪ ♪

59
00:10:39,279 --> 00:10:44,779
Far below on the forest floor,
only 2% of sunlight penetrates.

60
00:10:44,779 --> 00:10:48,779
It's not water that limits life;
it's light.

61
00:10:48,779 --> 00:10:53,279
For every 100,000 seeds,
only one will survive.

62
00:11:01,279 --> 00:11:04,779
Fewer still will ever
reach the canopy.

63
00:11:04,779 --> 00:11:09,779
They have to fight
for their place in the sun.

64
00:11:23,479 --> 00:11:29,440
Just half an inch can mean
the difference between life and death.

65
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:46,100
Each plant has its own strategy
to get ahead.

66
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:49,100
This struggle makes the jungle

67
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:53,100
one of the most competitive
environments on Earth.

68
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:56,600
A war in which every leaf matters.

69
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:07,100
In the dry season,
there's not much else to eat.

70
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:11,100
Plants fight back
with spikes and poison,

71
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:13,600
loading their leaves with toxin.

72
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:25,100
With each bite, their victims
become sicker and sicker.

73
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:29,100
There is an antidote,
but to reach it

74
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:55,680
they must face the jungle's
most dangerous predators.

75
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:04,440
Poisoned by the plants they eat,

76
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:08,440
these animals must reach
the antidote.

77
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:11,440
But it's a dangerous mission.

78
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:15,440
Ocelot, jaguars, and puma
are waiting.

79
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:27,440
A deadly game of hide and seek,

80
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:31,440
and at its heart,
a most unlikely cure: clay.

81
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:35,440
It's rich in the minerals and salts

82
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:38,440
needed to neutralize the toxins.

83
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:49,440
But the longer the dry season,

84
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:53,440
the more they must visit the clay.

85
00:14:08,170 --> 00:14:11,330
♪ ♪

86
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:19,560
With so much danger
on the forest floor,

87
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:23,560
it pays to keep off the ground.

88
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:44,560
This orangutan spends 90%
of her time in the trees.

89
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:49,560
As the heaviest arboreal species
in the world,

90
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:53,560
orangutans let their weight
do the work.

91
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:57,560
Tree swaying saves half the energy

92
00:14:57,560 --> 00:15:01,560
she would normally use to climb.

93
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:05,560
Shortage of food
in the dry season

94
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:08,560
forces her to rest more.

95
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:27,560
Each afternoon she makes her bed,

96
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:30,560
weaving branches into a nest

97
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:35,560
that will keep her safe
through the night.

98
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:40,560
And these trees provide more
than food and shelter.

99
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:45,560
Remarkably, they also help create
the jungle's weather.

100
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:05,560
By the end of the dry season,

101
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:09,560
the sun is at its most intense.

102
00:16:11,109 --> 00:16:14,609
Trees pump out more water vapor

103
00:16:14,609 --> 00:16:18,609
than at any other time of year.

104
00:16:26,609 --> 00:16:31,609
In this jungle,
almost 20 billion tons every day.

105
00:16:31,609 --> 00:16:35,609
All this water creates
the wet season here.

106
00:16:35,609 --> 00:16:38,609
But this jungle is shrinking,

107
00:16:38,609 --> 00:16:42,609
and its rainmaking power is fading.

108
00:16:50,609 --> 00:16:54,609
Every decade the change
from dry to wet

109
00:16:54,609 --> 00:16:57,609
comes a week later.

110
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:13,280
A mighty storm is brewing,

111
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:15,780
but before it strikes,

112
00:17:15,780 --> 00:17:19,280
there's a killing to be made.

113
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:38,480
Competition for food is so intense
during the day,

114
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:42,480
it has forced some creatures
into the night.

115
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:54,480
Spectral tarsiers.

116
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:58,480
To thrive in the dark,
they've evolved eyes

117
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:01,480
bigger than their brains,

118
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:05,480
and the best night vision
of any primate.

119
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:24,480
But they still need
a little help: a moon.

120
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:29,480
When it's full,
this family can catch more,

121
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:49,480
so they hunt for twice as long.

122
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:02,900
♪ ♪

123
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:08,880
But when storm clouds
obscure the moon,

124
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:13,880
others are better equipped
to kill in the shadows.

125
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:26,880
This python sees with heat
and smells with taste.

126
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:43,620
The tables turn again.

127
00:19:46,620 --> 00:19:50,620
Living in a group means
these tarsiers

128
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:54,120
can look out for each other.

129
00:19:59,270 --> 00:20:07,910
♪ ♪

130
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:14,480
With no element of surprise,
the python has no chance.

131
00:20:30,039 --> 00:20:34,039
But life is about to get tougher.

132
00:20:37,039 --> 00:20:40,039
The wet season has arrived,

133
00:20:40,039 --> 00:20:44,039
and it's hitting harder than ever.

134
00:20:57,120 --> 00:21:00,120
Before the wet season breaks,

135
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:05,120
there are more lightning strikes
in jungles

136
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:08,120
than anywhere else on Earth.

137
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:20,120
By 2050, some estimate
they will increase by a third.

138
00:21:39,279 --> 00:21:44,779
The storms these trees help create
can also be their downfall.

139
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:03,569
♪ ♪

140
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:51,100
The death of an emergent tree

141
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:56,100
is an essential part
of the cycle of life.

142
00:22:56,100 --> 00:23:00,100
The increased humidity
during the wet season

143
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:03,100
sets off a chain reaction.

144
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:13,600
Fungi and slime molds
race to decompose

145
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:16,840
dead matter on the forest floor.

146
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:36,760
Rot and decay run rampant
faster than anywhere else on Earth.

147
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:42,760
In some jungles, species of fungi
outnumber plants 33 to 1.

148
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:56,760
As they feed on the dead,
they recycle critical nutrients

149
00:23:56,760 --> 00:24:00,440
which the forest uses to grow.

150
00:24:09,039 --> 00:24:15,039
Many spread by releasing spores,
up to 30,000 a second.

151
00:24:15,039 --> 00:24:21,039
If just one of these spores lands
in the right place

152
00:24:21,039 --> 00:24:26,039
and takes root,
it can colonize a whole new area.

153
00:24:44,039 --> 00:24:49,039
But not all fungi feed on the dead.

154
00:24:59,919 --> 00:25:03,919
Days ago,
a spore landed on this ant.

155
00:25:03,919 --> 00:25:06,419
Now she's acting strange.

156
00:25:15,419 --> 00:25:19,419
A network of roots
has infiltrated her muscles.

157
00:25:19,419 --> 00:25:23,919
Her body has been taken over
by Cordyceps,

158
00:25:23,919 --> 00:25:25,919
a parasitic fungus.

159
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:37,140
It floods her brain
with chemicals,

160
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:40,640
drugging her, compelling her
to head

161
00:25:40,640 --> 00:25:43,640
where conditions are perfect.

162
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:47,140
Just the right amount of light,

163
00:25:47,140 --> 00:25:50,640
just the right amount of humidity

164
00:25:50,640 --> 00:25:53,640
for the parasite growing inside.

165
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:08,640
It forces her to clamp down
in a death bite,

166
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:12,640
and Cordyceps reveals
its gruesome nature.

167
00:26:32,200 --> 00:26:35,200
After 3 weeks of growth,

168
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:38,700
Cordyceps can release
its own spores,

169
00:26:38,700 --> 00:26:42,200
infecting more ants,
releasing more spores,

170
00:26:42,200 --> 00:26:45,700
infecting more ants,
releasing more spores,

171
00:26:45,700 --> 00:26:49,200
infecting more ants,
infecting more ants,

172
00:26:49,200 --> 00:26:52,200
more and more and more.

173
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:08,200
Cordyceps can wipe out
entire ant colonies.

174
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:12,700
But more than just ants
are at risk.

175
00:27:31,039 --> 00:27:35,039
There are over 600 species
of Cordyceps

176
00:27:35,039 --> 00:27:37,539
spread across the world.

177
00:27:37,539 --> 00:27:40,539
Most are found in jungles

178
00:27:40,539 --> 00:27:45,539
where they prey on
a whole host of victims.

179
00:27:52,780 --> 00:27:55,960
♪ ♪

180
00:28:04,279 --> 00:28:10,279
The wet season brings a flush
of fruit to the canopy.

181
00:28:17,279 --> 00:28:22,279
Lar gibbons must move fast
before it's all gone.

182
00:28:34,279 --> 00:28:39,279
They fly through the trees
at 35 miles an hour,

183
00:28:39,279 --> 00:28:42,279
even with a baby on board.

184
00:28:52,279 --> 00:28:57,279
They can cover 40 ft
in a single leap.

185
00:29:07,279 --> 00:29:12,279
But they don't get it right
every time.

186
00:29:12,279 --> 00:29:17,279
This family of lar gibbons
lives in a dangerous world.

187
00:29:17,279 --> 00:29:20,279
Their forest is being fragmented.

188
00:29:45,279 --> 00:29:51,279
One day they may face a jump
they can't quite make.

189
00:30:16,159 --> 00:30:22,159
Food is harder to find
as a wet season grows more erratic.

190
00:30:22,159 --> 00:30:27,159
And when the rain comes,
it can fall in shorter,

191
00:30:27,159 --> 00:30:29,159
more intense bursts.

192
00:30:41,159 --> 00:30:46,159
If it's too wet,
it's best to sit tight.

193
00:30:46,159 --> 00:30:51,159
This orangutan has learned
a lot from her mother:

194
00:30:51,159 --> 00:30:55,159
how to make a jungle umbrella.

195
00:30:55,159 --> 00:31:01,159
It comes in handy
in the rainiest environment on Earth.

196
00:31:15,159 --> 00:31:19,159
For many animals,
heavy rain stops activity.

197
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:35,600
But for some,
that's not an option.

198
00:31:35,600 --> 00:31:38,600
This male booted racket-tail
hummingbird

199
00:31:38,600 --> 00:31:42,100
lives on the brink
of starvation.

200
00:31:42,100 --> 00:31:47,100
Just two hours without nectar
and he could die.

201
00:31:47,100 --> 00:31:51,600
Hummingbirds have
the fastest metabolisms on Earth.

202
00:31:51,600 --> 00:31:56,600
Some need to visit
2,000 flowers a day

203
00:31:56,600 --> 00:31:59,100
just to keep going.

204
00:32:08,100 --> 00:32:13,100
This mountainous forest
is one of the few jungles

205
00:32:13,100 --> 00:32:15,600
that is getting wetter.

206
00:32:24,600 --> 00:32:28,100
Heavy rain is predicted
to increase,

207
00:32:28,100 --> 00:32:32,600
and when you weigh
less than a nickel,

208
00:32:32,600 --> 00:32:35,100
raindrops are a bombardment.

209
00:32:58,639 --> 00:33:01,639
Waterlogged feathers
slow his progress.

210
00:33:01,639 --> 00:33:04,639
Staying airborne
becomes more demanding.

211
00:33:04,639 --> 00:33:10,639
But he's running on empty,
and the clock is ticking.

212
00:33:20,639 --> 00:33:26,639
Even during a downpour,
competition for flowers is fierce.

213
00:33:38,639 --> 00:33:42,639
A buff-tailed coronet,
intent on keeping

214
00:33:42,639 --> 00:33:46,639
the nectar-filled flowers
for himself.

215
00:33:51,639 --> 00:33:56,639
The racket-tail is no competition
for the coronet.

216
00:33:59,919 --> 00:34:03,419
He must wait
for another opportunity.

217
00:34:07,419 --> 00:34:11,419
As the rains slow,
over 40 species

218
00:34:11,419 --> 00:34:14,419
fight for their nectar hit.

219
00:34:25,270 --> 00:34:29,619
♪ ♪

220
00:34:32,440 --> 00:34:36,440
With the coronet facing
bigger battles,

221
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:41,440
this is a racket-tail's chance
to sneak a sip.

222
00:34:41,440 --> 00:34:44,940
It takes more energy to hover

223
00:34:44,940 --> 00:34:48,940
than almost any other activity
on Earth.

224
00:34:58,940 --> 00:35:04,940
We'd have to drink
over a can of soda a minute

225
00:35:04,940 --> 00:35:06,940
to keep up.

226
00:35:12,940 --> 00:35:14,940
Another racket-tail.

227
00:35:14,940 --> 00:35:18,440
Evenly matched,
he won't back down.

228
00:35:18,440 --> 00:35:23,440
Tail splayed, feet forward,
he means business.

229
00:35:46,260 --> 00:35:49,749
♪ ♪

230
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:04,760
The winner takes all.

231
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:07,760
But he can't rest.

232
00:36:07,760 --> 00:36:12,760
He still has a lot
of flowers to visit,

233
00:36:12,760 --> 00:36:17,760
and the next downpour
is never far off.

234
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:29,760
Rainfall in the Andes
transforms life

235
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:32,760
over a thousand miles away.

236
00:36:40,760 --> 00:36:46,760
So much water collects
in the Amazon basin below

237
00:36:46,760 --> 00:36:51,260
that the Earth's crust
sinks by 3 in.

238
00:36:57,640 --> 00:36:59,640
A drowned forest.

239
00:36:59,640 --> 00:37:03,140
This extreme change takes months.

240
00:37:12,140 --> 00:37:17,140
Even so, it can creep up
on those

241
00:37:17,140 --> 00:37:21,140
who live their life
in slow motion.

242
00:37:30,740 --> 00:37:34,740
Moving between the trees
becomes challenging.

243
00:37:34,740 --> 00:37:38,740
She needs to find her next meal,

244
00:37:38,740 --> 00:37:40,740
but she's surrounded.

245
00:37:48,740 --> 00:37:55,740
Creatures that spend most of the year
on the forest floor

246
00:37:55,740 --> 00:38:00,740
now find themselves floating
30 ft above it.

247
00:38:07,740 --> 00:38:11,740
Their only refuge
is in the trees.

248
00:38:14,740 --> 00:38:18,240
But she must brave the deep.

249
00:38:30,720 --> 00:38:33,720
This sloth's home is flooded.

250
00:38:33,720 --> 00:38:37,720
To find her food,
she must swim,

251
00:38:37,720 --> 00:38:41,220
defenseless against
what lies beneath.

252
00:38:52,390 --> 00:38:55,780
♪ ♪

253
00:38:58,400 --> 00:39:02,900
Like most animals here,
sloths are adapted

254
00:39:02,900 --> 00:39:06,400
to get through
this annual flood.

255
00:39:06,400 --> 00:39:10,400
Fermenting leaves fill
her stomach with gas

256
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:13,400
that helps keep her afloat.

257
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:25,400
She's three times faster in water
than on land.

258
00:39:31,120 --> 00:39:37,120
When the forest floods,
it opens up a whole new world.

259
00:39:43,120 --> 00:39:46,120
Pink river dolphins can explore

260
00:39:46,120 --> 00:39:49,120
an area larger than Arizona.

261
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:07,420
They echolocate to hunt for fish
in the murk

262
00:40:07,420 --> 00:40:11,920
using higher frequencies
than their marine cousins

263
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:14,920
to see with superior definition.

264
00:40:14,920 --> 00:40:19,920
Recently, these floods have been
reaching record-breaking highs,

265
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:23,920
but there have also been
devastating lows.

266
00:40:33,920 --> 00:40:40,420
And as our world changes,
drought is the greatest natural threat

267
00:40:40,420 --> 00:40:42,420
to jungles worldwide.

268
00:40:42,420 --> 00:40:46,920
Australia was once covered
by a jungle

269
00:40:46,920 --> 00:40:50,420
larger than the Amazon rainforest.

270
00:41:00,420 --> 00:41:06,420
Now barely 1% survives,
clinging to what little water remains.

271
00:41:06,420 --> 00:41:11,420
And little red flying foxes
cling on with it.

272
00:41:11,420 --> 00:41:13,920
It's a 104°F.

273
00:41:13,920 --> 00:41:19,920
Just 4° more, and this male
will die of heat shock.

274
00:41:19,920 --> 00:41:23,420
He needs to escape the sun.

275
00:41:35,420 --> 00:41:40,920
But with hundreds of thousands
of bats in the colony,

276
00:41:40,920 --> 00:41:44,420
the shadiest spots are hard won.

277
00:42:06,460 --> 00:42:09,460
Exposed,
he's dangerously dehydrating.

278
00:42:19,460 --> 00:42:23,460
The river is their only salvation,

279
00:42:23,460 --> 00:42:27,460
but it can also be their ruin.

280
00:42:42,460 --> 00:42:47,460
These waters are infested
with freshwater crocodiles.

281
00:42:59,960 --> 00:43:02,460
Better to stay away.

282
00:43:02,460 --> 00:43:05,960
Try and hold out till nightfall.

283
00:43:05,960 --> 00:43:10,460
But with every breath,
he loses more water.

284
00:43:10,460 --> 00:43:15,460
More and more bats
give in to their thirst,

285
00:43:15,460 --> 00:43:18,960
and he won't last much longer.

286
00:43:28,960 --> 00:43:32,460
It's safer to share the risk.

287
00:43:32,460 --> 00:43:38,460
To collect water, they must dip
their fur in the river,

288
00:43:38,460 --> 00:43:42,460
but no one wants to be first.

289
00:44:01,170 --> 00:44:13,730
♪ ♪

290
00:44:16,050 --> 00:44:22,290
♪ ♪

291
00:44:56,040 --> 00:44:57,540
Safe.

292
00:44:57,540 --> 00:45:02,040
But he must brave this river
every day

293
00:45:02,040 --> 00:45:04,540
until the rains arrive.

294
00:45:04,540 --> 00:45:10,040
Over the next 50 years,
it could get too hot

295
00:45:10,040 --> 00:45:15,040
and dry for this colony
to survive at all.

296
00:45:15,040 --> 00:45:21,040
Could this be the future
for jungles around the world?

297
00:45:32,440 --> 00:45:37,440
These amazing forests
not only create oxygen and rain

298
00:45:37,440 --> 00:45:40,440
that nourish our planet;

299
00:45:40,440 --> 00:45:45,440
they're also home to a greater
diversity of animals

300
00:45:45,440 --> 00:45:48,440
than anywhere else on Earth.

301
00:45:48,440 --> 00:45:51,440
These creatures
are super specialized

302
00:45:51,440 --> 00:45:56,440
to survive all the complexities
of life in the jungle.

303
00:45:56,440 --> 00:46:02,440
But in times of change, that also
leaves them highly vulnerable.

304
00:46:02,440 --> 00:46:06,440
It takes years for an orangutan
to learn

305
00:46:06,440 --> 00:46:10,440
how to find its way
in these forests,

306
00:46:10,440 --> 00:46:15,440
and today's changing climate
makes life even tougher.

307
00:46:20,440 --> 00:46:25,440
And that isn't all
she has to contend with.

308
00:46:30,960 --> 00:46:33,960
Rainforests around the world

309
00:46:33,960 --> 00:46:37,960
are disappearing faster
than ever before.

310
00:46:50,960 --> 00:46:55,960
Her future, like that
of all jungle life,

311
00:46:55,960 --> 00:46:58,960
has never been less certain.

312
00:47:10,050 --> 00:47:21,889
♪ ♪

